# roms/

**No ROM byte is ever committed here.** `.gitignore` keeps everything in this
directory out of git except this file, and that rule is inherited from n64lle
rather than chosen per project.

Stage your own dump of **@NAME@** as:

```
roms/@ROM_BASENAME@
```

The build acts only on a dump matching the identity in `../game.toml`, which was
read off the dump this project was cut from on @DATE@:

| | |
|---|---|
| cart id | `@CARTID@` |
| region | `@REGION@` (@REGION_LABEL@) |
| CIC | `@CIC@` |
| size | @ROM_SIZE@ bytes (@ROM_SIZE_H@) |
| CRC1 / CRC2 | `@CRC1@` / `@CRC2@` |
| SHA-256 | `@SHA256@` |

Check a candidate before staging it:

```sh
sha256sum "your dump.z64"
# or, for the whole identity at once:
python3 ../n64lle/tools/new_project/probe_rom.py "your dump.z64"
```

A `.v64` or `.n64` dump is normalized to big-endian in memory when it loads, so
either will run — but the SHA-256 above is of the `.z64` file, and the launcher
verifies against exactly that, so a differently ordered dump will read as
unverified even though it boots.
